      {
        "id": 105282,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-29T03:22:47.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Really liking the look, too!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Now, can I see everything I want to be able to see at a glance? Not quite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I know this may be asking a lot, but I want to be able to see everything that I can see when I'm playing the game on a table. That includes things like what are both the maximum and current HP of a target and all of the cards in play (it looks like only two of a hero's cards can be shown). It also means being able to read the text of each card, though I'll admit that I can usually only do that by grabbing and reading the individual card, so something that allowed me to, for instance, touch a card to see its text might be sufficient.</p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:34:50.528Z",
