      {
        "id": 105283,
        "name": "MigrantP",
        "username": "MigrantP",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-29T12:27:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Frankly, it's impossible to show everything that you can see on the table in a game of Sentinels on a tablet screen. On a 50\" 4K TV, perhaps. We need to work within the capabilities we have. That means showing the most important information at a given time, while making it easy to see everything else you may need with as few interactions as possible.</p><p>On the screen posted here, you can scroll through the hero &amp; environment cards horizontally, and/or bring up the \"thought bubble\" view as seen in the previous post. And just as before you can bring up the full text of any card quickly.</p><p>However, as mentioned in the past, we are planning to include another screen (the \"overview\") that attempts to show as much information as possible. The overview can be activated at any time, and would show at least the title &amp; HP of all cards in play. Now you can imagine what can happen in a game of Sentinels and think about whether that screen could include artwork &amp; text.. the other day we played Matriarch and she had every single fowl in play.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:34:50.618Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
