        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Frankly, it&#39;s impossible to show everything that you can see on the table in a game of Sentinels on a tablet screen. On a 50&quot; 4K TV, perhaps. We need to work within the capabilities we have. That means showing the most important information at a given time, while making it easy to see everything else you may need with as few interactions as possible.</p><p>On the screen posted here, you can scroll through the hero &amp; environment cards horizontally, and/or bring up the &quot;thought bubble&quot; view as seen in the previous post. And just as before you can bring up the full text of any card quickly.</p><p>However, as mentioned in the past, we are planning to include another screen (the &quot;overview&quot;) that attempts to show as much information as possible. The overview can be activated at any time, and would show at least the title &amp; HP of all cards in play. Now you can imagine what can happen in a game of Sentinels and think about whether that screen could include artwork &amp; text.. the other day we played Matriarch and she had every single fowl in play.</p>",
